        "original_id": "282c1e88-b4e9-54ba-a700-845a905173d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Khalid Latif, Sharjeel Khan, Nasir Jamshed, Mohammad Irfan, Shahzaib Hasan, Mohammad Nawaz\n- Organizations: Pakistan Cricket Board, PCB\n- Events: 2004 U-19 Cricket World Cup, 2010 Asian Games, 2017 Pakistan Super League spot-fixing scandal\n- Roles: Opening batsman, captain\n- Topics: Spot-fixing, cricket suspensions, cricket bans\n\nFacts:\n- Khalid Latif is a right-handed opening batsman.\n- Khalid Latif captained Pakistan to victory in the 2004 U-19 Cricket World Cup.\n- Khalid Latif captained Pakistan to a bronze medal in the 2010 Asian Games.\n- In the 2017 Pakistan Super League spot-fixing scandal, the PCB suspended Sharjeel Khan and Khalid Latif on 10 February 2017.\n- In the 2017 Pakistan Super League spot-fixing scandal, the PCB suspended Nasir Jamshed on 13 February 2017.\n- In the 2017 Pakistan Super League spot-fixing scandal, the PCB suspended Mohammad Irfan on 14 March 2017 and Shahzaib Hasan on 17 March 2017.\n- In the 2017 Pakistan Super League spot-fixing scandal, the PCB suspended Mohammad Nawaz on 16 May 2017.\n- In 2017, the Pakistan Cricket Board banned Khalid Latif from all forms of cricket for five years for his involvement in spot-fixing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
